FOUNDERS LEDGER
Sunday, September 20, 2026 | Edition 90

Good morning. Four things this week.

1) ROUNDS WE NOTICED
- Orchard Robotics (Fresno) raised a $35M Series A led by Cormorant Capital for tree-crop harvesting robots.
- Stillwater Compliance (Minneapolis) closed an $11M seed led by Alder Lane Ventures for environmental-permit tracking.
- Kindling Health (Nashville) announced a $20M Series A led by Palisade Growth for home-health scheduling.
- Harrow Analytics (Boston) raised a $9M seed from Granite Peak Ventures for insurance-claims analytics.

2) TERM SHEET WATCH
Tranched rounds are back for hardware. Four of the nine hardware Series As we saw this month were structured as two closes, with the second tranche tied to a milestone (usually a first production unit or a signed pilot). Software rounds are still single-close. If you are offered a tranche, negotiate the milestone definition harder than the valuation; a vague milestone is a re-negotiation with extra steps.

3) CHART OF THE WEEK
Extension and bridge rounds as a share of all A-stage financings: 34% in the first half of 2026, the highest reading in our data. Half of the extensions were priced flat to the prior round; a quarter were down. Chart: https://foundersledger.com/charts/extensions-h1-2026

4) WORTH READING
"The board deck that takes two hours to build," on a five-slide monthly format that a dozen founders now use, and why the fifth slide is always the ask. https://foundersledger.com/reads/two-hour-board-deck

Have a good Sunday.
Colette

